        {
          "title": "Caching, Async and Scheduling Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Proxy-Based AOP",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Caller",
                    "sub": "another bean",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Spring proxy",
                    "sub": "intercepts call",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Extra behaviour",
                    "sub": "cache, thread, timer",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Real method",
                    "sub": "your code",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Opt-in switches on a ==@Configuration== class: `@EnableCaching`, `@EnableAsync`, `@EnableScheduling`",
                "No switch = annotations {red:silently ignored}"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. When the Proxy Is Skipped",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`this.method()` self-invocation: `@Cacheable`, `@Async`, `@Transactional` do nothing",
                "`private` methods are not intercepted; use ==public==",
                "`final` class or method cannot be proxied",
                "Object must be a ==Spring-managed bean==, not `new`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "public User first() {",
                "    return this.get(1L); // no proxy",
                "}",
                "@Cacheable(\"users\")",
                "public User get(long id) { ... }"
              ],
              "note": "get() always runs; call it from another bean"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Cache Facade",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==CacheManager== hands out named `Cache` objects",
                "Provider is swappable; annotated code stays unchanged"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "@Cacheable",
                    "sub": "annotation",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "CacheManager",
                    "sub": "facade",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cache users",
                    "sub": "named cache",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Caffeine or Redis",
                    "sub": "provider",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Go through the proxy",
              "text": "Call the annotated method from **another bean**. A call inside the same class is {red:never intercepted}."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cacheable, CacheEvict and CachePut Workflow",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cacheable, CacheEvict and CachePut Workflow",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The @Cacheable flow",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Call",
                    "sub": "through proxy",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Lookup",
                    "sub": "cache + key",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "x",
                    "text": "Hit",
                    "sub": "body skipped",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Miss",
                    "sub": "run, then store",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`@Cacheable(\"users\")` checks the cache ==first==",
                "Default key = **all arguments** (`SimpleKey` if none)",
                "Override with SpEL: `key = \"#id\"` or `key = \"#user.id\"`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Three annotations",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Annotation",
                "Method runs?",
                "Cache effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`@Cacheable`",
                  "only on a miss",
                  "reads, or fills"
                ],
                [
                  "`@CachePut`",
                  "{green:always}",
                  "refreshes the entry"
                ],
                [
                  "`@CacheEvict`",
                  "always",
                  "removes the entry"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`@CacheEvict(value = \"users\", key = \"#id\")` removes ==one entry==",
                "`allEntries = true` clears the **whole cache**",
                "`@CachePut` suits ==update methods==",
                "Mixing `@CachePut` and `@Cacheable` on one method"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Condition, unless, example",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`condition = \"#id > 0\"`: checked **before** the call",
                "`unless = \"#result == null\"`: checked **after**, skips storing"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@Cacheable(value=\"products\", key=\"#id\",",
                "           unless=\"#result==null\")",
                "Product find(Long id) { ... }"
              ],
              "note": "null results are never cached"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "==condition== = before the call. ==unless== = after the call, so it can read `#result`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cache Providers: Caffeine vs Redis",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cache Providers: Caffeine vs Redis",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Two Providers",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Caffeine",
                "Redis"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Where",
                  "In-process",
                  "Out-of-process, shared"
                ],
                [
                  "Speed",
                  "==Fastest==, no network hop",
                  "Network + serialization cost"
                ],
                [
                  "Instances",
                  "Own copy each, entries {red:drift}",
                  "{green:Consistent} across instances"
                ],
                [
                  "Restart",
                  "Cache lost",
                  "Survives"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Configuration",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Caffeine: one ==spec== string sets size and expiry",
                "Redis: needs `spring-boot-starter-data-redis` and a ==serializer== (JSON or Serializable)",
                "Per-cache TTLs need a custom `RedisCacheConfiguration`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "properties",
              "lines": [
                "spring.cache.type=caffeine",
                "spring.cache.caffeine.spec=maximumSize=500,expireAfterWrite=10m",
                "spring.cache.type=redis",
                "spring.cache.redis.time-to-live=10m"
              ],
              "note": "use one type at a time"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Choosing",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Caffeine}: hot, small, read-mostly data on one node",
                "{orange:Redis}: multi-instance or large shared data",
                "Combine as a ==layered== cache"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "L1 Caffeine",
                    "sub": "local, fastest",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "L2 Redis",
                    "sub": "shared",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Database",
                    "sub": "source",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why do Caffeine entries drift?** Each instance keeps its own copy; nothing syncs them.",
                "**Why is Redis slower?** Every call pays a network hop plus serialization.",
                "**Per-cache Redis TTL?** Define a custom `RedisCacheConfiguration`.",
                "**What is L1/L2?** Caffeine in front of Redis, Redis in front of the database."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Async Methods and Executors",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Async Methods and Executors",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What @Async Does",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "On a public bean method: ==returns immediately==, body runs on an executor thread",
                "Return `void`, `Future` or `CompletableFuture<T>`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Caller",
                    "sub": "calls proxy",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Proxy",
                    "sub": "submits task",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Executor thread",
                    "sub": "runs body",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Executors",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Setting",
                "Value"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Default bean",
                  "`applicationTaskExecutor` (ThreadPoolTaskExecutor)"
                ],
                [
                  "Default sizing",
                  "core ==8==, queue **unbounded**"
                ],
                [
                  "Named pool",
                  "`@Async(\"mailExecutor\")`, slow jobs cannot starve others"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@Async(\"mailExecutor\")",
                "public CompletableFuture<Void> send(Mail m) {",
                "    mailer.deliver(m);",
                "    return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(null);",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "runs on the mailExecutor bean's threads"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Pitfalls",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`void` exceptions never reach the caller: set an `AsyncUncaughtExceptionHandler`",
                "With `CompletableFuture`, inspect it: `exceptionally` or `get()`",
                "Security context is thread-bound: it is ==not propagated==",
                "Transaction is thread-bound: @Async starts a ==fresh transaction=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Name your pool, return `CompletableFuture`, and handle errors. Caller context does not follow the thread."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Scheduled Tasks and Thread Pool Pitfalls",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Scheduled Tasks and Thread Pool Pitfalls",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Triggers",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Attribute",
                "Timing"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`fixedRate=5000`",
                  "every 5s, ==start to start=="
                ],
                [
                  "`fixedDelay=5000`",
                  "5s after the previous run ==finishes=="
                ],
                [
                  "`initialDelay`",
                  "postpones the first run"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@Scheduled(cron = \"0 0 2 * * *\", zone = \"Asia/Kolkata\")"
              ],
              "note": "second minute hour day month weekday: daily 02:00 in that zone"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Pool pitfalls",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Default scheduler is {red:single-threaded}: one slow job delays all others",
                "Fix: `spring.task.scheduling.pool.size` or a `TaskScheduler` bean"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Core threads busy",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Queue fills",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Grow to max",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Reject",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Unbounded queue== never fills, so `maxPoolSize` never applies",
                "Set `queueCapacity`; use `CallerRunsPolicy` for ==back pressure=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Shutdown and nodes",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`setWaitForTasksToCompleteOnShutdown(true)` plus an awaitTermination period",
                "Several instances: lock jobs with ==ShedLock== so only one node runs each"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Spring Caching, Async and Scheduling Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Spring Caching, Async and Scheduling Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Switches and the proxy",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`@EnableCaching`, `@EnableAsync`, `@EnableScheduling` on a @Configuration class",
                "Calls must go through the ==proxy==: `this.method()` skips it",
                "Method is ==public== on a Spring bean"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Cache annotations and providers",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Annotation",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`@Cacheable`",
                  "reads, or runs and fills"
                ],
                [
                  "`@CachePut`",
                  "always runs, refreshes"
                ],
                [
                  "`@CacheEvict(allEntries=true)`",
                  "clears the cache"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "SpEL: `key=\"#id\"`, `condition` before the call, `unless=\"#result==null\"` after",
                "{blue:Caffeine}: local, fast, `maximumSize=500,expireAfterWrite=10m`",
                "{red:Redis}: shared, `time-to-live=10m` plus a serializer"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Async and schedule",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`@Async(\"mailExecutor\")` on a public method, return `CompletableFuture`",
                "Bounded `queueCapacity` plus a rejection policy such as `CallerRunsPolicy`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mode",
                "Timing"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`fixedRate`",
                  "start to start"
                ],
                [
                  "`fixedDelay`",
                  "end to start"
                ],
                [
                  "`cron`",
                  "6 fields plus `zone`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Several instances",
              "text": "Lock jobs with ==ShedLock== or every node runs them."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`twice(1)` calls `get(1)` two times inside the same bean, and `get` has `@Cacheable`. How many times does the body of `get` run?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Twice: `this.get()` bypasses the proxy",
                "No cache lookup happens, so nothing is ever stored",
                "Fix: call from another bean, or move `get` out"
              ],
              "example_code": [
                "@Cacheable(\"x\") public int get(int id) { ... }",
                "public int twice(int id) { return get(id) + get(id); }"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "An executor has core 2, max 10 and the default queue. You submit 20 slow tasks. How many threads run?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Only 2: the default queue is unbounded and never fills",
                "So the pool never grows past core, and `max` is ignored",
                "Set `queueCapacity` to let it grow"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A `fixedRate=5000` job takes 8s on the default single-threaded scheduler. When does each run start?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Every ~8s, right when the previous run ends",
                "Runs never overlap; late ones start immediately",
                "`fixedDelay=5000` would give 13s gaps"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
